Stainless example programs
SPDX-License-Identifier: 0BSD

The programs in this directory are under the Zero-Clause BSD licence, not
the GNU General Public License that covers the rest of Stainless.

They exist to be copied. The runtime library exception in
../LICENSE.RUNTIME does not help here: it permits combining the *runtime*
with your own code, whereas lifting a sample means copying its source, and
a GPL'd source file would carry its licence into whatever you pasted it
into. Zero-Clause BSD asks for nothing at all -- no attribution, no notice,
no copyleft -- so a snippet taken from here stays yours.

The same applies to the test programs in ../tests/cases/, several of which
are copies of these samples; it would be odd for one file to carry two
licences depending on which directory it sits in.

Nothing else changes. Stainless itself remains under the GPLv3
(../LICENSE), and its runtime library under the GPLv3 with the additional
permission in ../LICENSE.RUNTIME.

